"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[14828],{414828:e=>{e.exports="# Salesforce\n\n## Guidelines\n\n> **IMPORTANT** — You help the user **set up Salesforce ingestion in Databricks**. **Do not write data to Salesforce or otherwise modify the customer's Salesforce org** (no creates, updates, deletes, or configuration changes via APIs, Bulk jobs that mutate data, or scripts). **Read-only** operations are **expected and appropriate** here—including SOQL/query-style checks, listing objects, schema inspection, and other diagnostics that **only verify credentials and data or object accessibility** without changing org state. If something would alter Salesforce, tell the user to do it in Salesforce or through supported Databricks flows—not via assistant-driven mutations.\n\n## Setting Up Salesforce\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- A Salesforce **Connected App** with OAuth enabled\n- The integration user must have **API Access** enabled on their profile\n- The integration user must have **read access to each object** being ingested — object-level permissions alone are not sufficient if field-level security (FLS) restricts specific fields\n\n### Configuration Notes\n\n- The connector uses the Salesforce REST API; **Bulk API 2.0** is used for large data exports\n\n## Diagnosing Salesforce Connection\n\n### Diagnostic Flow\n\n1. **Validate credentials** — call `salesforce_validateCredentials`. If error, credentials may have expired.\n2. **Check object access** — call `salesforce_checkObjectAccess`. If 404/403, user lacks permissions.\n3. **List objects** — call `salesforce_listObjects` to see all queryable objects.\n4. **Get object schema** — call `salesforce_describeObject` to verify field-level access.\n5. **Check data** — call `salesforce_getRecordCount` to verify records exist.\n\n## Source Reference\n\n### Objects and Fields\n\nSalesforce organizes data as **objects** (equivalent to tables). Standard objects include `Account`, `Contact`, `Lead`, `Opportunity`, `Case`, `Task`, `Event`. Custom objects have names ending in `__c` (e.g., `My_Object__c`).\n\nCommon starting points to suggest to users:\n\n- `Account` and `Contact` — core CRM entities, highest value for most analytics use cases\n- `Opportunity` — sales funnel and revenue reporting\n- `Case` — customer support and service analytics\n- Custom objects vary by org — use `salesforce_listObjects` to show what's available\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- Objects with >500K records are high risk for performance issues; Bulk query jobs may time out on very large datasets\n- **Field-level security (FLS)**: fields restricted by FLS are invisible to the API user even if the object is accessible — a field missing from the schema usually means FLS, not a missing object permission\n- Bulk API 2.0 jobs are asynchronous; failures during the job (not at submission) may not surface immediately\n"}}]);
